          "widgets": {
            "faqs": [
              {
                "question": "Do I need to book a ticket?",
                "answer": "We encourage everyone to book a free ticket as it helps us to manage visitor numbers but you are welcome to turn up without a ticket to see the exhibition (on the days we are open). Please notify us if you are visiting in a group larger than 6 people."
              },
              {
                "question": "Do I need to book a ticket for a specific time slot?",
                "answer": "No. Please select \"10am\" on the date that you'd like to visit, and you can visit at any time during exhibition opening hours on that day. We'd recommend to arrive at least 1 hour before exhibition closing time, so you have the opportunity to see everything."
              },
              {
                "question": "How long does it take to view the exhibition?",
                "answer": "It takes about an hour to view the exhibition. There are additional optional items to view  for as long or as little as you like such as the two digital galleries on London Picture Archive about Agatha Christie’s London and Crime and Punishment in the 19th century, and a selection of reference books"
              },
              {
                "question": "Tell me more about my donation.",
                "answer": "Thank you for your support! A small donation can make a big difference to our work to preserve and share London's archives by helping us to deliver outreach and learning activities, develop free exhibitions and care for the collections."
              },
              {
                "question": "Questions about accessibility?",
                "answer": "The exhibition is held on the first floor and is accessible by stairs and a lift. An accessible toilet is adjacent to the exhibition space. Further details: www.thelondonarchives.org/visit-us/accessibility . Please contact ask@tla.libanswers.com if you have any specific queries about access needs. "
              },
              {
                "question": "Do you offer curator-led tours?",
                "answer": "We will be running curator-led tours on selected dates - these are available to book for £5 on the event listing:  https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/curator-led-exhibition-tour-londoners-on-trial-tickets-1982025153589?aff=oddtdtcreator"
              },
              {
                "question": "Are group visits possible for adults?",
                "answer": "Groups of 7 or more people need to make special arrangements to visit so we can manage capacity - please contact ask@tla.libanswers.com to make a group booking. In addition, we may be able to offer curator-led tours of the exhibition for groups for a small charge, depending on staff availability."
              },
              {
                "question": "Are school group visits possible?",
                "answer": "Interactive learning sessions about Crime and Punishment can be booked for Key Stage 2 classes and take place in our Learning Studio. These can be combined with a visit to the exhibition - please indicate on the booking form. More details: https://www.thelondonarchives.org/learning/primary-schools"
              },
              {
                "question": "Do you have a cafe?",
                "answer": "We don't have a cafe on site, but we're located right next to Exmouth Market, which has lots of good options for coffee and lunch."
              },
              {
                "question": "Are you open on weekends or Bank Holidays?",
                "answer": "The exhibition is free to visit during our normal opening hours on Mondays, Tuesdays, Wednesdays, Thursdays and one Saturday per month. We are closed on all Bank Holidays and during our Annual Closure (Friday 14 - Monday 31 August) and our Christmas Closure (Thursday 24 Dec - Sunday 3 January)."
              }
